<article class="enc-article">
<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amir Barid I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1542</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amir">Amir</a> Barid I was the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qasim-barid">Qasim Barid</a> and the second ruler of the Barid dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bidar">Bidar</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a>. Like his father he controlled the last Bahmani sultans as chief minister, and after the last of them fled around 1527 he ruled Bidar in his own right. His son Ali Barid Shah was the first of the family to take the title of shah.</p></div>
